{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]I just pulled onto the highway in my little foreign car.
[D]Well, it's rainin' an' the road is really bad.
[D]I never saw that big ol' diesel but I heard him hit the air.
I've got a feelin' that I [A]might have made him [D]mad.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]He closed the gap between us, pushed the pedal on the floor.
[D]He's makin' ninety in that big ol' diesel truck.
[D]I can hear the names he's callin' me above the engine's roar,
An' the words won't be found in [A]Webster's [D]book.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]There's a diesel on my tail a-makin' ninety miles an hour.
